title a renamed directory carrying a subtree

# No fixture in the corpus renames a directory that still has live
# children, so the theory's implicit-descendant rule has never been
# exercised by either emission compiler.
#
# Section 12: "Under full-path naming, a directory rename implicitly
# renames every decided descendant, so descendant edits are
# expressed against the post-rename paths." So after /d becomes /e,
# the child is ALREADY at /e/f -- and an explicit rename of
# /d/f to /e/f would name a source that no longer exists.
#
# But a compiler that works pool by pool sees 3-100's names change
# from /d/f to /e/f exactly as it sees 2-100's change from /d to /e,
# and has no reason to treat one differently. Whether the descendant
# rename should be emitted, suppressed, or emitted and skipped by
# check-then-act is the question this fixture asks.
#
# Onto is quiet, so nothing conflicts and nothing is held.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: d/
      3-100: f = fv0

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: d/
      3-100: f = fv0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: e/
      3-100: f = fv0
